From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:56:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iPhone film speed: keep films read for ten minutes, start the
 head read before the token (rule 1811)

FilmModel.publicFilm: kept films (600 s, 60 at most), else the read under way, else
fetchPublic (rule 1535 unchanged: no token, logged, one retry). init starts the read, so it
no longer waits for FilmScreen's auth.accessToken(); load and loadRead join it. Rule 1535's
check now counts the calls through publicFilm. Not compiled here (Linux).

